WEBVTT

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.910
Again?

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.520
Hey, Big Sis!

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.980
You gotta wake up,
or you'll be late for school!

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.230
I'm up...

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.370
You really aren't...

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:57.030
Mom!

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.180
Coming!

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.740
Koharu.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:09.170
If you don't wake up soon,
you won't have time...

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.170
...to braid your hair.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.050
Oh, no!

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:18.510
No! No! That'd be awful!

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:20.790
Good morning.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:22.560
Good morning...

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.160
Very cute.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.730
Thank you, Mom.

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.460
You're quite welcome.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.760
Time to eat!

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.470
Our little glutton is still waiting.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.980
Oh, sorry!

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.510
You finally got to eat,
Wanpachi!

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.940
Sota, if you have time to spare,
you could help out!

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:22.490
I can't! Wanpachi only eats
the Pokémon food <i>you</i> put out.

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.620
It really is strange...

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:30.260
Out of everyone in the family,
Koharu acts the coldest towards Wanpachi, and yet...

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.540
Coldest?

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:38.550
I suppose Koharu is the one Wanpachi
loves and cares for the most out of us all.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:40.320
Really?

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.690
Who's second, then?

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:44.440
That would be m-

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.310
Mom!

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.440
Why, thank you, Wanpachi!

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:52.020
I'm its third favorite!
Right, Wanpachi?

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.320
So I'm dead last...

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.540
We're off!

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.470
See you later!

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.790
Hey, Wanpachi, cut it out!

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.160
That tickles!

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.780
Sit down.

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:24.260
PocketMonsters

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.680
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.260
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.980
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.850
And skip the slow send-off

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.190
Be it through fire or through water

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:39.860
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:44.360
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:49.620
Each and every one of my memories

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:54.210
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:58.130
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:03.880
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.890
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.100
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.440
Let's have a fight!

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:19.150
1: Once the battle's done

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.980
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.320
On 3, let's be friends!

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.990
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:37.330
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.830
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:43.960
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.760
I choose you!

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:54.770
the Occasional Gänger
Koharu, Wanpachi and

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.970
Satoshi, who dreams of
becoming a Pokémon Master...

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:04.540
And Go, who aims to
catch every Pokémon.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.630
What kind of Pokémon
will they meet today?

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:11.080
This is Sakuragi Institute.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:17.330
The Pokémon that Satoshi and Go caught
live comfortably in this vast garden.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:22.320
<i>Good morning, everyone!</i>

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.370
You sure caught a lot of Pokémon.

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:35.890
I've still got a long way to go!
There are <i>so</i> many more I <i>haven't</i> caught!

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:40.560
That's true. I wanna battle and
catch loads more, too!

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.570
Of course!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:45.780
Speaking of which...
Where's your Kairyu?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.480
What are they doing?!

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.920
Let's wait and see.

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:09.990
See?

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.360
Wow, you were right!

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:15.570
Yeah?

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:17.850
What's wrong, Pikachu?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:31.230
T-That's...

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.370
We gotta stop them!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.120
Yeah!

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:42.050
They're evolving!

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:43.420
Evolving?!

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:47.890
All right! Kemusso has
a split evolutionary line.

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:50.510
First it evolves into
either Karasalis or Mayuld,

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:55.130
And then Karasalis becomes Agehunt,
while Mayuld becomes Dokucale!

00:06:55.130 --> 00:07:00.520
That's why I caught
three Kemusso!

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.570
The first one's a Mayuld!

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.780
The second's a Mayuld, too!

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:14.880
The next one's gonna
become Karasalis, I'm sure!

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.580
M-M-Mayuld?!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.690
All three of them?!

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:28.140
Oh... well.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.080
All right...

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.600
What, a blackout?

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:45.690
Here we go...

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.610
Gotta find the switchboard...

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.660
Cold...

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:07.840
Come on, li'l Françoise!

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.070
Will you let me know
if you find any problems?

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:33.110
A-A p-poltergeist?!

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.260
Gänger?!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.320
Françoise!
Thunder Wave!

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:44.460
Oh! Are you all right?!

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.060
All right, see you later.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.420
Yeah. Have a nice day.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.560
I win!

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:05.630
Satoshi... You're so quick!

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.020
Koharu!

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.940
Morning, Koharu!

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:12.360
Good morning.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.790
Director!
My Kemusso evolved!

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:16.700
I see!

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:20.660
That was the first time
any of my Pokémon evolved!

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:26.410
It was, like, really touching...
Really made me feel how wonderful Pokémon are, yeah?

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:30.560
Hey, Koharu! Wanna come see
my freshly evolved Mayuld?

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.420
I'll introduce you to my Kairyu, too!

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:36.220
B-But I have to go to school...

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.220
Oh. I guess you're right.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.660
Good morning.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.430
Better hurry,
or you'll be late, Koharu.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.650
Of course! See you later, then!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:45.900
Take care.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:46.690
Bye!
Take care.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.250
Later!

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:54.900
Director, I have a question
about the latest project...

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.120
Got it. Let's talk in the main room.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.780
Say, Go...

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.790
Isn't Koharu
interested in Pokémon?

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.600
She wasn't like this before,

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:08.490
but nowadays, she's kinda cold...

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:09.570
Cold?

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:13.580
Well, people have different ways
of interacting with Pokémon.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:16.590
You and I are different, too.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:17.760
I guess.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.690
It's pretty dark.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.800
The door was wide open, too.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:29.090
Françoise?!

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:30.060
What's wrong?!

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.070
Oh, no!

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.210
Renji, hang in there!

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:47.910
Gänger?!

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:57.880
Is there something there?

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:06.770
What's that?!

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:11.690
Gänger! Shadow Pokémon!
Ghost/Poison type!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.910
It can pass through other dimensions
and can appear anywhere!

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.630
It steals heat from its surroundings.

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:21.030
If you feel a sudden chill,
it is certain that a Gänger appeared.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.740
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:43.970
100,000 Volts!

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.180
PocketMonsters

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.760
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:07.530
PocketMonsters

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:12.450
. Steel .
Electric
Coil
PocketMonsters

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:16.960
Have you all thought
about your futures?

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:21.720
Today, I thought I'd have you announce
your dreams for the future.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.370
"When I grow up,
I want to do this",

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:28.720
or "When I'm an adult, I want this job"...
That kind of thing.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:32.060
I'm really bad at
this kind of class...

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:34.980
All right, who wants to go first?

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.360
Well, then, Yuto!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.410
What? Me?

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.750
What is your dream for the future?

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:45.920
My dream is...

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.120
...a work in progress!

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.180
I see.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.120
Well, then, next... Koharu!

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.180
A-All right.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:58.600
You're so lucky that
your future's already set.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:01.260
Hey, Pokémon Professor!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:06.010
Oh, you're following in
your dad's footsteps?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:07.390
Um...

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:11.140
You gotta have loads of Pokémon
at home, right? Lucky you!

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.360
Just Wanpachi...

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.570
Really?!

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:17.590
Hey! Can we have
a Pokémon battle later?

00:13:17.590 --> 00:13:19.370
I've never done that before.

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:24.400
Is it really <i>that</i> surprising...?

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.280
Wait, do you hate Pokémon?

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:30.240
No, it's not like that...

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.930
Then, you like them?

00:13:31.930 --> 00:13:33.160
Like?

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:36.420
<i>Do</i> I like them?

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:40.770
Okay, that's enough
questions for Koharu!

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.120
Koharu.

00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:55.470
Mom! What are you doing here?

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:56.850
You forgot this.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:58.840
My lunch!

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:03.360
And then?

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:09.290
They were all, "Since you're a Pokémon Professor's daughter,
you must be good at battling" and stuff like that...

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:10.870
I didn't like that.

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.200
Of course you wouldn't.
That's really not nice.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:20.940
People thinking I <i>have</i> to love Pokémon,
or deciding my future for me...

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.160
Yup, yup.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:26.490
I don't know what my dreams
for the future are yet.

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:28.780
Say...

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:32.760
When did you decide you
wanted to be an illustrator?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:38.180
When you were a kid?
Or only after you'd grown up?

00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:44.110
Actually, back when I was in high school,
I wanted to be a comic artist.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.840
I didn't know!

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.760
I really tried.

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:52.900
I drew loads of drawings and practiced hard
to become a comic artist.

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:55.510
But I couldn't do it.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:15:02.700
Then, at some point,
I thought I should just give up on that dream.

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:03.460
What?

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.340
And then...

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:11.360
Aren't you going to draw today?

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.900
What? Um...

00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:16.100
Your comics.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:20.010
Oh... I figured it was time to
move on from that...

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:21.590
Why?!

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:24.190
You always looked like you were
having so much fun drawing them!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:27.110
What? Having fun?

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.110
Yes, that's right!
That's how it looked to me!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:37.000
So please don't just
move on from drawing so easily!

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:42.800
You became an illustrator
because Dad told you to?!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.450
No.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.220
I just thought that
he had a good point.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.140
I was the one who
made the choice, of course.

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:54.890
I see.

00:15:55.710 --> 00:15:58.030
It's not the comic artist
goal I once had,

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:00.790
and I'm by no means
a <i>famous</i> illustrator...

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:03.900
But I'm still having fun drawing.

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:12.410
The day will come when
you decide for yourself what you want to do.

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:14.570
I hope you're right.

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:19.420
You're still only ten.
There's no need to rush!

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.170
Gänger!

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.300
I wonder where it went.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:35.700
Hey, Satoshi! Let's compete to see
who can catch it first!

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:37.200
All right, you're on!

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:40.990
There!

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:43.810
Come on! Monster Ball, go!

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.690
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.660
It's hopeless...

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.490
Watch out, Barrierd!

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.500
You're amazing!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.460
Nice!

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:25.100
Iron Tail!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:32.440
Dodge!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.040
Hibunny, can you thaw it?

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:55.550
Electroweb!

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:08.940
Professor, what's this?

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.780
A diagram of the temperature
in the institute.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:16.120
If there's a rapid temperature drop somewhere,
that's probably where Gänger is.

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.450
I see.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.280
Now we can find it
even if it turns invisible!

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:22.810
Hey, Gänger!

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:26.040
Don't let your guard down, Go!
That Gänger's tough!

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:33.230
I'm home.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.270
Oh! I'm back, Wanpachi!

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:43.890
Yes, yes, that's enough.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:50.020
The lobby!
Gänger is in the lobby!

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:02.730
Wanpachi!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:16.880
Pikachu!
100,000 Volts!

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:38.650
Wanpachi?!

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.630
Wanpachi! Use Spark!

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:00.330
It seems it can't hear you.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:04.580
It's completely focused
on protecting Koharu.

00:20:04.580 --> 00:20:07.600
Koharu! Command Wanpachi
to use Spark!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.230
If <i>you</i> command it,
I'm sure it'll listen!

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.310
But I've never done this before!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:16.700
Wanpachi is desperately trying
to protect you!

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:23.740
Koharu is the one Wanpachi
loves and cares for the most out of us all.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:27.170
You can do it, Koharu!

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:28.120
Koharu!

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.880
Wanpachi! Spark!

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:52.990
Wanpachi did it!

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:54.720
Koharu,
that was awesome!

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.860
Wanpachi!

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:13.030
Thank you for today, Wanpachi.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.530
Hey! That tickles!

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:21.420
I said it tickles, Wanpachi!

00:21:27.690 --> 00:21:30.060
That Gänger sure was tough!

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.510
Yeah! I really wanna catch it!

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:38.280
Let's compete again
the next time we meet it!

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:39.170
Yeah!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:45.950
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.320
Let's play Pokémon Shiritori!
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.460
(Pikachu →<b> Mew Ver.)
Let's play Pokémon Shiritori!
Pokémon Shiritori</b>

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:50.030
Pokémon Shiritori
(Pikachu →<b> Mew Ver.)</b>

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:50.040
(Pikachu →<b> Mew Ver.)
Pokémon Shiritori</b>

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:50.290
Pokémon Shiritori
Pokémon Shiritori
(Pikachu →<b> Mew Ver.)</b>

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:51.580
Pikachu!

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.450
Utsubot!

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.160
Transel!

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:53.960
Lugia!

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.750
Achamo!

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:55.540
Morpeko!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.250
Koduck!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.130
Cleffy!

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:57.830
Eevee!

